eeger's the one guy mookie betts hasn't  done much here so  uh bellinger hasn't done much there's a  lot of fingers if you're uh you're  pointing for uh fingers of blame here  tom  yeah it's a great point because yeah i  mean we love talking about  the pitching decisions or manager  decisions on pitchers right  but that's a great point they really  have not hit you think about the guys  who have shut them down you know after  that big outburst in in game three it  was  noah a 22 year old right-hander with  very little major league experience and  last night you had this kid bryce wilson  who pitched an  unbelievable game had seven career  starts  22 years old hadn't pitched in a weekend  with two weeks and a half  so it you know they're not seeing cy  young winners shutting them down maybe  it's just they're not familiar with  these guys but  a big load has to go to the dodger  offense because it was number one in  baseball  this year i also wondered about this  when i was  looking at the nba bubble you saw a lot  of young teams do well because  you didn't have to travel to staples and  play in front of a hostile crowd  you're playing in a basically sterile  environment there  these younger players and the braves had  a lot of younger players  they're there in the they're not a  dodger stadium they're there in  arlington  there's no real you know home field  disadvantage here there's no bullying or  none of that  feels like that plays right into the  braves that it's a young team  they may not know better and they're not  intimidated by any of this  i'm with you especially when it comes to  the pictures there's no question about  that actually last night when the game  started of the nine people on the field  for the braves  five of them were 23 and younger and  they're shutting down  you know this juggernaut of a team  because the dodgers in the regular  season were a juggernaut  i'll tell you because i've been in the  bubble i'm down there it feels like a  college or high school atmosphere  because  the families are really close to the  field here in arlington  there's 11 000 people they're scattered  around it's really not that loud they  still have some fake crowd  noise in there but they're all saying  hello to mom and dad or the girlfriend  it really feels like an american legion  tournament so you're right i think it  does help  especially these young pitchers i mean  you put them in dodger stadium 50  000 people you know triple deck that's a  different atmosphere  than a bubble if uh this doesn't work  out for the dodgers  what happens with dave roberts if  anything  i don't think anything happens really  okay um  you know again it depends how it ends  the next couple of days  if it does i still i'm not counting them  out then i mean this is a really really  good team you saw the way they broke out  in the first inning the other night i'm  not saying they're going to score 11  again  um but man that the lineup is due to  break out with something here at some  point beyond what they did in that one  inning so  i'm not ruling them now it's gonna be  difficult don't get me wrong bullpen day  for the braves today and then you've got  frieden anderson  and i think both those two guys are  legit no matter sweet is probably the  tougher matchup for the dodgers but both  those guys are really good  that curveball is i you know i hadn't  seen much of him but i  i when i watched him i was like oh my  gosh  you know i'm glad you mentioned that  because the way they've shut down the  dodgers here overall  you know the one exception this is not a  high velocity team  we love talking about fastballs and the  dodgers have a million guys coming out  of the bullpen throwing literally a  hundred miles an hour  if you lined up the 16 playoff teams the  braves are  13th in average velocity so you've got  freed with that curveball he's added the  slider you've got anderson with that  killer  changeup i thought wilson did a great  job mixing up his pitches  they're not beating the dodgers with  velocity or pure stuff they're pitching  this group and  you have to give them credit for being  so young and this good  what advice would you give the astros  when it comes to questions about 2017  uh i go full on nuke lelouch and be as  dull and boring as possible  right don't take the bait because you  know what happened in that first  first round with minnesota right carlos  correa they got through minnesota he's  like oh we're back you know we're like  the bills you want to get rid of us you  can't get rid of us  i think some guys talk to him because  the next round they were like  very chill about it i think that's the  way i would hand it don't give anybody  any more  ammunition you've done plenty of that  already and altuve's had a couple of big  hits  are his throwing woes that that was only  one game there  uh no but i can tell you a story here  before that series  the raised scouts in their hitters  meeting before the series  they said when you hit a ground ball to  second base even a routine one  bust it down the line we're not sure if  this guy's gonna make the play  so they saw something there with his  body language how deliberate he was the  arm whatever it was  they put those guys on notice so if you  notice choi  and lao busted it down the line on  routine balls and put pressure on him  i'm not sure that goes away that quickly  dan  and you've been around long enough that  we had chuck knoblock and we have steve  sacks mackie sasser couldn't throw the  ball back to the mound  did you ever do i'm sure you did but um  like talk to a psychologist or  somebody who would look at this and say  what happens in the brain  when you know rick ang kills another one  yeah it's when  athletes start to think right they start  to think about the process the lack of  thought you hear that from hitters all  the time right i wasn't thinking  anything just see the ball hit it you  know it's funny the guy pitching when he  pitched in relief last night for the  braves tyler matsuk  he had the yips as a pitcher right he  was out of baseball former number one  pick out of baseball  it took him a year going to see  psychologists  uh psychiatrists uh throwing every day  on his own  and it took him another year in the  minor leagues independent ball to get  back  i think more guys just don't get back  it's really hard to get back from it and  it seems to affect  second baseman as you mentioned there  and the occasional pitcher  but it's an odd throw from second base  it's like an odd throw when a comebacker  goes to the mound the pitcher  is he's guiding it shortstop in third  you have to  unleash it you know it's rare when you  get you know a looper that you can throw  in there second was always  odd and and i was a former shortstop so  you get it you fire second sometimes you  fire sometimes you lob it and it feels  like  sometimes you're right in between well i  think you're on something there when you  have a little bit of  extra time that clock tells you have a  little bit of time that's when the brain  starts to get in the way  of the muscles right if you're a  shortstop in the whole third base  long throw you don't have time to think  about it second baseman knows he has  time and i think that's  that works against them if i would have  told you when uh  the marlins had their outbreak that they  were going to make the playoffs what  would you have said  no way i mean really i mean don  mattingly did an  incredible job with that team i mean you  think about they had 18 people out  uh i think it was 174 roster moves they  went through they had 20 guys make their  major league debuts  in a 60 game season i mean it was crazy  but you know listen that young group  found itself  mattingly did a great job their young  pitching is legit i didn't think it  would come this quickly but  again dad you made the point about  nobody in the stands i think that helped  them  it was sort of a bonding experience too  to go through what they did  but bottom line was i think mattingly  has to be the manager of the year for  the job that he did with that group  uh have fun tonight there nine eastern  on uh fox sports one  and uh it'll be braves and dodgers again  do you think we're gonna live to see  another game i do  i i can't count out the dodgers uh you  know what i think it's a low scoring  game tonight again though because that  braves bullpen  it's a bullpen game brian snickers got a  lot of good options  so you know most cases most teams are up  against it with the bullpen game not the  braves  thank you tom i know you're busy we  appreciate you making some time for  us yeah dan have a good one that's tom  verducci sports illustrated  senior writer working for fox sports and  mlb

